  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youths as Agents of Positive Change Using Sports and Interactive Media</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">St.Johns Sports Society (SSS) based at St. John&apos;s sub - parish of Kariobangi has worked with communities of Korogocho slums in Nairobi for over 20 years. Korogocho slum is a low-income inhabited by a population of over 100,000 residents.   In this project, SSS proposes to take forward and consolidate the gains of the partnership it has had with CAFOD since 2008 in supporting communities in Korogocho mainly through Sports, arts and cultural performances aimed at mobilizing youth towards constructive use of their skills and talents for justice and peace.  
For the next two years, the project seeks to use sports and culture as tools to bring change among in Korogocho slums within the framework of peace and justice agenda. The project shall use youths participating in different sports and cultural activities as agents of change. Our key strategies will include use of various sport teams (football, netball, volleyball, karate, tae-kwondo, handball and boxing), education and leadership teams and media programmes (electronic and print). 
There will also be training of pupils and teachers on peace education in order to address early warning signs to elections related conflicts.  600 peace builders will also be trained. A music festival and roadshows will be conducted to mobilize communities 
Direct beneficiaries will be about 250 members of various sports teams and about 600 new members who will be recruited in the next three years.  The indirect beneficiaries will be about 37,000 residents of Korogocho slum.</narrative>
  </description>
